I walk further across the market.
Suddenly I can smell fresh bread.
I follow the good smell over to a baker.
He has freshly baked, dark rye bread.
There is a little sign in front of the bread.
"Does it cost forty kroner?" I ask.
The baker nods.
I give him a hundred-kroner note.
He hands me the warm bread.
"Here you go, and sixty kroner back," he says.
I say thank you and put the bread in my bag.
It feels lovely and warm.
